  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ (as shown in the table below) and the cumulative distribution function $F(y),$ compute $F(3).$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ |\n\n$F(3)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=0)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.20+0.25 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
